              "chunkIndex": 3,
              "text": "a few kelvins below its initial value.\nMagnotherm uses an active magnetic regenerator (AMR) to increase the cooling span, with a water-based fluid circulating through the system.\nThe unit includes a magnetocaloric material block, an AMR with control valves, a rotating permanent magnet assembly, a fluid pump, electronic controls and two water-air heat exchangers for cooling and heat rejection.\nThe study/scalability: Magnotherm partnered with a supermarket chain that operates tens of thousands of propane display cases to pilot a 0.4kW (0.1TR)-capacity Eclipse by installing the unit in a retrofitted R290 cabinet.\nIn the 11-week study, running from May to September, the retailer confirmed that the Eclipse cabinet used 15% less energy than the incumbent propane cases, while maintaining the target temperature of 4‒5°C (39.2 to 41°F).\n“The customer plans to deploy a minimum of 10 more Eclipse units in supermarkets next year,” Sirman said.\nThe magnetocaloric technology has the potential to offer a cooling capacity range from 0.1 to 500kW (0.3 to 142.2TR), according to Sirman, with different materials providing a temperature range from −270 to 160°C (−454 to 320°F).",
